    "findings": [
      "Verified every one of the 56 fixed-scope files against its recorded SHA-256; the 12 Headtaker formal pages and their current shared/index relations are stable.",
      "The six supported weapon families map to six trait variants and 16 actual bindings. Current weapon-family/pattern/mark labels, reverse pages, map rows, trait/item restrictions, template attachments, and the icon path/attachment identity agree; the combataxe_p1 label update is limited to names and does not alter mechanics or values.",
      "The six own tier/wrapper records support the listed per-stack melee-power values: five families use 3.5/4/4.5/5 percent and the heavy-sword family uses 6.5/7/7.5/8 percent. The matching melee_power_level_modifier replaces the child fallback; the child has five effective stacks, and the shared 3.5-second inactivity window clears all effective stacks while accepted capped hits refresh that window.",
      "The player text and action matrix correctly distinguish eligible melee hits from pure push, document actual direct-special follow-ups, and exclude all nine verified chainaxe sticky profiles that set skip_on_hit_proc. The first qualifying hit resolves before its event and cache update, so it cannot benefit retroactively; later actions use the updated cache. Switching pauses the held-gated contribution while the shared timer continues; actual unequip/removal clears the effect.",
      "The tier reconstruction uses the exact paired RAW keys and formatter behavior for all eight family/tier rows. Tier numbers, five stacks, and 3.5 seconds agree with implementation; mechanics omitted by RAW are classified as 「文件未涵蓋」. The README no longer contains an empty or generalized errata section, and the localization comparison retains the RAW-versus-implementation classification with the corrected reconstruction punctuation.",
      "The power examples define B after the weapon power-type curve and before the merged additive modifier. Results 625, 700, and 725 (with q=20 percent) are arithmetically correct and are explicitly power-input results, not claims of fixed final damage.",
      "The restored first-effect recovery receipt is narrowly scoped to the first-hit/cache-order question and does not claim restoration of the missing historical Opening Salvo addendum; the config and draft preserve that provenance."
    ],
